Package: scimagR
Title: Spinal Cord Injury Imaging Pipeline for MRI and CT Analysis
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("R.", "Heller", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                   email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
                   comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: An end-to-end pipeline for longitudinal magnetic resonance
    imaging (MRI) and computed tomography (CT) analysis in spinal cord injury
    (SCI) research. Provides R wrappers for the 'Spinal Cord Toolbox' (SCT;
    De Leener et al. (2017) <doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2016.10.009>),
    including 'SCIsegV2' lesion segmentation, DICOM anonymization and NIfTI
    conversion helpers built on 'pydicom' and 'dcm2niix', SCI-specific
    clinical metrics (maximum spinal cord compression, compression ratio,
    tissue bridge quantification), implant artifact grading, and pipeline
    orchestration with built-in quality control. Integrates with
    'workflowr' for reproducible, publication-ready neuroimaging analyses.
    All external tools are optional; the metrics, registry, quality-control
    and plotting functions work without them.
